## 🛠️ Essential Tools & Network Diagnostic Insights
*   **Telnet:** A powerful plaintext terminal interface client used manually to craft application headers and test raw text connections to remote server listening ports.
*   **Wireshark:** A network packet analyzer. Because legacy protocols like FTP, POP3, and Telnet transmit all credentials and payloads in **unencrypted plaintext**, Wireshark acts as an indispensable "X-ray machine" to audit, intercept, and visually trace strings passing through a network card.

